    {'slug':'neural-driving-neuroevolution','title':'Neural Driving — Neuroevolution','domain':'AI · Control · Optimization','hero':'neural-driving.png','fit':'contain','summary':'Vehicle dynamics, nine range sensors, an explicit 10→12→8→3 MLP and genetic optimization of all 263 parameters.','report':'neural-driving-report.pdf','metrics':[('10→12→8→3','MLP architecture'),('263','optimized parameters'),('2 → 33','two-lap finishers / 50'),('14.41 s','replayed two-lap champion')], 'sections':[('Controller','Nine range sensors plus normalized speed feed a fully connected MLP that outputs steering, throttle and brake. No global racing line or absolute position is given.'),('Optimization','The network is evolved with tournament selection, elitism, uniform crossover, Gaussian mutation and random immigrants. No backpropagation is used.'),('Results','In the principal 10-generation experiment, finishers rise from 2 to 33 out of 50 and collisions fall from 48 to 17. Winning two-lap time improves from about 15.49 s to 14.45 s, then to about 14.41 s after a speed-deficit fitness refinement.'),('Limits','The main limitations are single-track training, simplified vehicle physics, a memoryless policy and sample-inefficient genetic search.')]},
